.TH "GALAXY\-LOGIN" "1" "" "galaxy" "Scalar Galaxy Manual"
.SH "NAME"
galaxy\-login \- sign in and save credentials
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B galaxy login
[\fB\-\-flow\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIurl\fR] [\fB\-\-environment\fR \fIname\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Obtains a credential and saves it so later commands do not have to carry one. It goes into your operating system's credential store \- the Keychain on macOS, the system keyring on Linux, Credential Manager on Windows \- and falls back to a file in your state directory, readable only by you, when no such store is available. Either way it is filed under the base URL it was captured for, so a credential saved for one host is never sent to another. A credential passed with a flag, or set in the environment, still takes precedence over a saved one.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-flow\fR \fIname\fR
Sign\-in flow to use, skipping the prompt. One of: bearer\-auth, basic, api\-key\-header, api\-key\-query, api\-key\-cookie, oauth\-client\-credentials, oauth\-password, open\-id\-connect.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIurl\fR
Sign in against this base URL instead of the default.
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\fR \fIname\fR
Sign in to the named environment instead of the default. One of: production, void. Falls back to SCALAR_ENVIRONMENT. Cannot be combined with \-\-base\-url.
.SH "SIGN\-IN FLOWS"
.TP
\fBbearer\-auth\fR
Enter your access token.
.TP
\fBbasic\fR
Username and password for basic auth.
.TP
\fBapi\-key\-header\fR
Enter your API key.
.TP
\fBapi\-key\-query\fR
Enter your API key.
.TP
\fBapi\-key\-cookie\fR
Enter your API key.
.TP
\fBoauth\-client\-credentials\fR
Sign in with a client id and secret (OAuth client credentials).
.TP
\fBoauth\-password\fR
Sign in with a username and password (OAuth password grant).
.TP
\fBopen\-id\-connect\fR
Paste an access token you already have.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
galaxy login
galaxy login \-\-flow bearer\-auth
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.TP
\fB10\fR
Sign\-in or sign\-out did not complete. The message on standard error says why.
